==''Blade''==
[[File:Bladeanime1.jpg|thumb|150px|right|Cast of ''Blade'', Eric Brooks]]{{Anchor|Blade (2011 TV series)}}
{{see also|List of Marvel Anime episodes#Blade|l1=List of ''Marvel Anime'' episodes § Blade}}
{{nihongo|'''''Blade'''''|[[:ja:ブレイド (2011年のアニメ)|ブレイド]]|Bureido}} (DVD title: '''''Blade: Animated Series''''') is the fourth and final show of the series. Comprising twelve episodes like the others, the story is written by [[Kenta Fukasaku]], son of the late [[Kinji Fukasaku]]. [[Jamie Simone]] served as casting director, reversion producer, and voice director for the English version where he was assisted by [[Mary Elizabeth McGlynn]]. It aired on Animax from July 1, 2011, to September 16, 2011. The entire series was released on DVD in the United States on July 31, 2012. It was also released on Blu-ray in Japan on February 22, 2012.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ja:ブレイド {{!}} ソニー・ピクチャーズ公式|url=https://www.sonypictures.jp/he/951518|access-date=2021-03-30|website=www.sonypictures.jp}}</ref>

===Plot===
Blade is a "daywalker" [[Vampire hunter|vampire hunter]] who was born with [[Dhampir|human and vampire]] blood in his veins after a vampire attacked his mother. Blade is visiting Japan on a mission where he not only confronts [[Deacon Frost]], the vampire who had killed his mother [[Vanessa Brooks|Tara Brooks]], but also goes up against a mysterious organization of vampires, known as "Existence".<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2011-06-01/blade-fairy-tail-ro-kyu-bu-promo-videos-streamed|title=Blade, Fairy Tail, Ro-Kyu-Bu! Promo Videos Streamed|date=July 17, 2023 |publisher=Anime News Network}}</ref>

